The fact-check established that "ballot applications" in the 2020 U.S. presidential election context refer to [vote-by-mail request forms](https://chicagoelections.gov/voting/vote-mail). However, the documented evidence only defines these terms and does not contain any information about an actual incident of an individual receiving multiple applications and voting multiple times, nor does it cite any official investigations or reports on such a case. Therefore, based solely on the provided record, there is insufficient information to verify or refute the claim.